question:
Using "price_fill.xlsx" and "material_unit_price.XLSX" as data sources, with Specification/model as the matching key and the Material Description column as the content to match against, fill the matched Unit price column values into the "Price" column in Sheet1 of "price_fill.xlsx".

 Matching rules: Use the "Specification/model" column in "price_fill.xlsx" as the match value, and perform fuzzy matching against the "Material Description" column in "material_unit_price.XLSX"; English letter case does not affect matching;
 If a row in "price_fill.xlsx" cannot find a corresponding matching key in "material_unit_price.XLSX", the Price column for that row retains its original value (if originally empty, it remains empty); if the same matching key has multiple records in "material_unit_price.XLSX", take the Unit price value from the last record;

 After filling is complete, save the result back to Sheet1 of "price_fill.xlsx", without changing the order or content of any other existing columns and rows.

